  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`, and `python -m pytest tests/test_types.py -q` passes (49 passed, 2 skipped).\n\n- **Class:** `KeyValue` is a `ParamType` subclass in `src/click/types.py`, right after `UUIDParameterType`. Its `name` is `\"key_value\"`. It splits on the first `=` only, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")` and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- **Errors:** input with no `=`, or with an empty key, calls `self.fail(...)` with `'<value>' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- **Export:** the class itself (not an instance) is exported from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_types.py` now covers valid pairs, the invalid inputs `abc`, an empty string and `=value`, and an end-to-end `@click.option(\"--set\", type=click.KeyValue())` command.\n\n`convert()` returns a non-string value unchanged, so an already-parsed tuple passes through as-is.",
